**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 
- `ui-smoke`: 
- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.NkDispersionChartTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests`
- `unit-tests`: `BerremanTests.RhoWithDispValueTests`, `BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests`

**How to implement.** Langasite's dispersive gyration becomes data, so that the engine Langasite preset can be stated as a `MaterialComplexity` once step 13 derives `properties` from the complexity (001 §B 'Physics is pure data'; .spec-md §3.2). The section brief does not name it; the deviation is recorded in `.history`. `FsxAcceptanceTests` stores the engine preset itself as a library material (`OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/FsxAcceptanceTests.fs:386`) and compares the table with `LangasiteOnSilicon.fsx`, whose film is that preset (`Berreman/Analytics/StandardSystems.fs:40-53`). `RhoWithDispValue` (`Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs:RhoWithDispValue`) carries only `DispersionFormula` components, while the preset's ρ (`Berreman/OpticalProperties/Dispersive.fs:58-63`, `rhoLa3Ga5SiO14`) is diag(i·g₁₁(λ), 0, i·g₃₃(λ)) with the transcendental g₁₁ and g₃₃ of `:40-49`. The kernels MOVE into the core, as S1.1 step 8 moved the index laws, so one implementation exists. (1) `Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs`, after `GyrotropicValue` and before `RhoWithDispValue`: `PublishedGyrationLaw`, a one-case union `LangasiteGyrationLaw` with `member value : int` = 1, `static member tryOfWire (v : int) : PublishedGyrationLaw option` (`None` for any other tag) and `member rhoAt (w : WaveLength) : Rho`. Its body is `g11La3Ga5SiO14`, `g33La3Ga5SiO14` and `rhoLa3Ga5SiO14` moved verbatim, reading the two Langasite `PublishedIndexLaw` cases as step 8 left those lets. `RhoWithDispValue` gains `PublishedLawRho of PublishedGyrationLaw`, and its doc names the case. (2) `Berreman/OpticalProperties/Active.fs:146-156`: `toRhoWithDisp` answers `RhoWithDisp law.rhoAt` for the case, and its doc says so. (3) `Berreman/OpticalProperties/Dispersive.fs`: `Langasite`'s `rhoWithDisp` (`:70`) is `RhoWithDisp LangasiteGyrationLaw.rhoAt`, and the three lets are deleted. Every engine number is unchanged, because the same expressions are evaluated. (4) Every match follows the case. A published law is data the editor ladder cannot carry. `MaterialComplexityEditError` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs:182-187`) gains `PublishedGyrationNotEditableErr of reason : string`. `ofComplexity`'s active arm answers it, naming the law, and its `caption` arm is added at `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs:372-375`. `MaterialComplexity.isEditable` (`MaterialComplexityEditor.fs:MaterialComplexity.isEditable`) answers false when the active aspect is a published law, so such an entry opens view-only. The gyration-class and handedness facets (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs:materialGyrationClassDef`, `materialHandednessDef`) still apply to it but extract no value, because a published law has no editor class and no handedness field. `gyrationComponentsOfComplexity` (`OpticalConstructor.Ui/NkDispersionChart.fs:164-167`) answers `allGyrationComponents` for it. (5) The built-in Langasite keeps the constant uniaxial gyration its seed carries, so no library number moves. The doc of `langasiteComplexity` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs:langasiteComplexity`) says so and names the published law as the engine preset's ρ. The comment at `OpticalConstructor.Tests/PropagationTests.fs:464-469` no longer says the ρ has no value-tree form. (6) Facts. `Berreman/BerremanTests/RhoWithDispValueTests.fs` gains two. `The langasite gyration law reproduces the engine Langasite rho`: at 400, 500, 600, 800 and 1000 nm, Im ρ₁₁ and Im ρ₃₃ of `LangasiteGyrationLaw.rhoAt` MUST equal, with exact `Assert.Equal`, G17 literals the worker records from `rhoLa3Ga5SiO14` before moving it; every other entry and every real part MUST be zero; and `(PublishedLawRho LangasiteGyrationLaw).toRhoWithDisp.getRho w` and `langasiteOpticalProperties.rhoWithDisp.getRho w` MUST equal `rhoAt w` through `MatrixComparison`. `The published gyration law round-trips its wire tag and refuses an unknown tag` covers the tag. `OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialComplexityTests.fs` gains `a published gyration law keeps a complexity view-only and refuses to seed the editor`: for a constant isotropic eps with `active = Some (PublishedLawRho LangasiteGyrationLaw)`, `isEditable` MUST be false and `ofComplexity` MUST be `Error (PublishedGyrationNotEditableErr _)`. `OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryFacetsTests.fs` gains `a published gyration law offers the activity facets but extracts no class or handedness`, over an entry built by `materialEntryWith` (`:85-93`). `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs` gains `a published gyration law opens the editor view-only`: `initMaterialEditor` over such an entry MUST give `ViewOnlyMaterial _`. `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/NkDispersionChartTests.fs` gains `a published gyration law draws every gyration component`: `gyrationComponentsOfComplexity` of that complexity MUST equal `allGyrationComponents`.

**Acceptance.** After the gyration law lands, unit-tests (RhoWithDispValueTests, EpsWithDispValueTests) MUST pass with the two new facts and the law equal to its literals; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass with the MaterialComplexityTests and LibraryFacetsTests facts; ui-tests (MaterialEditorWindowTests, NkDispersionChartTests, FsxAcceptanceTests) MUST pass with the two new facts and both LangasiteOnSilicon facts; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the four s02 invariants MUST pass.
